      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "Template::Plugin::HTML versions through 3.102 for Perl allows HTML and JavaScript to be injected.  The html_filter function did not escape single quotes. HTML attributes inside of single quotes could be have code injected.  For example, the variable \"var\" in      <a id='ref' title='[% var | html %]'>  would not be properly escaped. An attacker could insert some limited HTML and JavaScript, for example,      var = \" ' onclick='while (true) { alert(1) }'\"  Note that arbitrary HTML and JavaScript would be difficult to inject, because angle brackets, ampersands and double-quotes would still be escaped.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
